│ patch_description        │ Replace the random Gaussian sample with a deterministic multi-start optimizer for the     │
│                          │ actual scale-invariant diameter-packing objective.  The optimizer maximizes a             │
│                          │ differentiable soft approximation to the log of the minimum pairwise distance minus the   │
│                          │ log of the maximum pairwise distance, gradually sharpening that approximation so that the │
│                          │ final iterations concentrate on active closest and farthest pairs.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each restart is centered and RMS-normalized only to remove the objective’s translation    │
│                          │ and scaling null directions; this does not impose a unit-cube or unit-sphere constraint.  │
│                          │ The best candidate is selected using the evaluator’s exact squared distance ratio rather  │
│                          │ than the smoothed training objective.  Fixed seeds make the returned 14-point             │
│                          │ configuration reproducible.                                                               │
