│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_diameter_packing                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the unstructured Gaussian sample with a deterministic multi-start optimization    │
│                          │ for the diameter-normalized packing problem.  The points are repeatedly centered and      │
│                          │ scaled so their current diameter is one; the optimization then maximizes the smallest     │
│                          │ separation.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A smooth surrogate is used during optimization: a soft minimum emphasizes short pairs and │
│                          │ repels them, while a soft maximum emphasizes long pairs and pulls them together.          │
│                          │ Temperature annealing makes the final iterations increasingly close to the actual         │
│                          │ minimum/maximum-distance objective.  Several reproducible random initial configurations   │
│                          │ are tried, and the configuration with the best true squared ratio is returned.  This      │
│                          │ directly targets the evaluator metric while retaining translation, rotation, and scale    │
│                          │ invariance.                                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
