│ patch_name               │ diameter_packing_search                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the unstructured Gaussian sample with a deterministic multi-start local search    │
│                          │ for the 14-point diameter-packing problem.  The search directly optimizes the evaluator’s │
│                          │ squared objective, `min_squared_distance / max_squared_distance`.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each candidate is centered and normalized to unit diameter, which is valid because the    │
│                          │ objective is invariant under translation and uniform scale.  The update uses weighted     │
│                          │ repulsion from near-minimum-distance pairs and weighted attraction for near-diameter      │
│                          │ pairs, plus a small reproducible annealed perturbation to escape poor contact graphs.     │
│                          │ Multiple seeded restarts are retained, and the best exact pairwise ratio is returned.     │
│                          │ This constructs exactly fourteen finite 3D points without relying on external             │
│                          │ optimization packages.                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
