│ patch_name               │ basin_hopping_polish                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Add a second, low-temperature basin-hopping polishing phase after the broad multi-start   │
│                          │ search. The existing annealing stage is effective at locating a near-optimal packing, but │
│                          │ its relatively high-temperature trajectory can stop slightly away from the nonsmooth      │
│                          │ optimum determined by a small active set of shortest and diameter pairs.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added phase perturbs the best incumbent by a small reproducible amount and            │
│                          │ re-optimizes it with a much sharper soft-min/soft-max approximation. This specifically    │
│                          │ searches nearby contact-graph variants while retaining the incumbent unless a strictly    │
│                          │ improved true squared ratio is found. Diameter normalization is retained after every      │
│                          │ move, so the new search remains in the same translation/scale quotient space and always   │
│                          │ returns exactly fourteen finite 3D points.                                                │
