│ patch_description        │ Add a short second-stage continuation after each broad soft optimization restart. The     │
│                          │ existing schedule ends at beta=120, which still averages several nearly active closest    │
│                          │ and diameter pairs. For a diameter-packing optimum, the final improvement is controlled   │
│                          │ by the exact contact graph, so a higher-beta stage better approximates the true           │
│                          │ minimum-distance versus maximum-distance objective.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The Adam state is reset before this stage because the earlier broad-force momentum is no  │
│                          │ longer appropriate once only contact pairs matter. The reduced learning rate avoids       │
│                          │ disrupting the already good configuration while allowing contact constraints to settle.   │
│                          │ This is a targeted refinement that preserves the existing restart strategy and            │
│                          │ normalization invariances.                                                                │
