│ patch_name               │ exact_ratio_basin_polish                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation uses a different hybrid strategy: smooth continuation is used only to │
│                          │ discover promising contact graphs, explicit diameter-constrained SLSQP is used to sharpen │
│                          │ those graphs, and a final batched exact-ratio basin polish accepts moves only when the    │
│                          │ evaluator’s actual squared ratio improves.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The final stage is deliberately based on the nonsmooth true objective rather than a       │
│                          │ surrogate. It proposes many centered, RMS-normalized tangent perturbations at once,       │
│                          │ evaluates the exact minimum-pairwise-distance squared divided by                          │
│                          │ maximum-pairwise-distance squared, and adaptively shrinks the search radius when no       │
│                          │ strictly improving move exists. This helps resolve close contact changes that smooth      │
│                          │ soft-min formulations can leave slightly suboptimal.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
