│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ diameter_contact_balance                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Augment the fixed-diameter repulsive relaxation with an explicit far-contact attraction   │
│                          │ term. The current force only increases the soft minimum distance, relying on              │
│                          │ renormalization to handle the diameter. Near the final high-beta regime, this can leave   │
│                          │ the active diameter pair poorly balanced against the nearest-neighbour contact graph.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added soft-max weight identifies current and near-current diameter pairs. Attracting  │
│                          │ those pairs with a scale proportional to the current squared ratio supplies the missing   │
│                          │ derivative of a soft minimum-distance divided by soft diameter objective. This provides   │
│                          │ intermittent contact-graph balancing throughout the late continuation without changing    │
│                          │ the exact SLSQP formulation used for final certification and polishing.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
