│ patch_description        │ This version combines a broad stochastic contact-search phase with an explicit            │
│                          │ diameter-packing feasibility solve and a final exact-ratio contact-exchange polish. The   │
│                          │ initial phase uses continuation on a smooth log-distance contrast to discover several     │
│                          │ distinct contact graphs. The strongest configurations are then rescaled so their shortest │
│                          │ distance is one and polished by directly minimizing the squared diameter under all        │
│                          │ pairwise lower- and upper-distance constraints. Finally, a small deterministic/random     │
│                          │ tangent perturbation stage accepts only strict improvements in the evaluator’s actual     │
│                          │ squared ratio, allowing small contact graph adjustments that smooth objectives and        │
│                          │ constrained solvers can miss.                                                             │
