│ patch_description        │ Resetting Adam’s accumulated moments when the soft-contact objective becomes              │
│                          │ substantially sharper prevents momentum fitted to broad pair distributions from           │
│                          │ destabilizing newly active closest and farthest contacts. The replacement also uses a     │
│                          │ more conservative learning-rate multiplier and longer second-moment memory at high beta   │
│                          │ values.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A short final backtracking phase then operates directly on the best exact candidate. It   │
│                          │ alternates sharp soft-contact sets and accepts only changes that improve the evaluator’s  │
│                          │ actual squared-distance ratio, so it cannot degrade the best candidate obtained by the    │
│                          │ population search.                                                                        │
