│ patch_description        │ Replace the final stochastic soft-force polishing with explicit contact-aware moves. The  │
│                          │ objective is nonsmooth: only shortest-pair and diameter-pair memberships matter locally.  │
│                          │ This edit forms separate near-minimum and near-maximum active sets, alternates a          │
│                          │ shortest-contact repulsion move with a diameter-contact contraction move, and retains     │
│                          │ small random perturbations solely for contact-graph exchanges. Every move remains subject │
│                          │ to strict exact-ratio acceptance, so this cannot degrade the best retained configuration  │
│                          │ while providing more decisive local refinement than a single force whose competing        │
│                          │ contacts can cancel.                                                                      │
