│ patch_name               │ contact_set_polish                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final softmax-only polishing stage with an exact contact-set method. At a     │
│                          │ near-optimal packing, the useful geometry is concentrated in several tied or nearly tied  │
│                          │ shortest and diameter pairs; a very sharp softmax can arbitrarily emphasize one of them.  │
│                          │ The replacement explicitly forms both active sets, pushes endpoints of short contacts     │
│                          │ apart, pulls endpoints of diameter contacts together, and accepts only strict             │
│                          │ improvements of the evaluator’s actual squared ratio. Small deterministic tangent         │
│                          │ perturbations are tested alongside the contact direction, allowing contact-graph changes  │
│                          │ that a single smooth gradient cannot initiate. Since every accepted candidate is compared │
│                          │ against the exact score, this cannot discard the previously found packing.                │
