│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ constrained_diameter_polish                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a final two-pass SLSQP diameter formulation after the existing smooth and exact-score │
│                          │ searches.  The objective can be written with the minimum squared separation fixed to one: │
│                          │ minimize the squared diameter `q` subject to every pair satisfying `1 <= d_ij^2 <= q`.    │
│                          │ This directly matches the evaluator ratio, unlike the smooth contact surrogate.           │
│                          │ Rescaling between passes reinitializes the active set at an exactly normalized minimum    │
│                          │ distance, and the final candidate is retained only when its measured exact ratio improves │
│                          │ the incumbent.  Analytic constraint Jacobians keep the small constrained solve practical. │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
