│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ contact_set_polish                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final softmax-only backtracking stage with an explicit active-contact method. │
│                          │ The exact objective is nonsmooth: at a good packing, several shortest pairs and several   │
│                          │ diameter pairs are usually tied, so a softmax can dilute the useful direction or choose   │
│                          │ an unstable subset of ties. The replacement forms separate near-shortest and              │
│                          │ near-diameter contact sets, applies a balanced force that expands the short contacts      │
│                          │ while contracting the diameter contacts, and periodically proposes tangent random         │
│                          │ directions to permit contact-graph exchanges. Every proposal is still accepted only when  │
│                          │ the evaluator’s exact squared ratio strictly improves.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The contact bands cycle from narrow to wider tolerances. Narrow bands sharpen an          │
│                          │ established active graph; wider bands allow nearly active constraints to participate      │
│                          │ before they become limiting. Removing translation and radial-scale components from random │
│                          │ proposals preserves the meaningful degrees of freedom.                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0413                                                                                   │
