│ patch_name               │ antipodal_linepacking                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This uses a geometric reduction rather than directly optimizing 14 unconstrained points.  │
│                          │ The 14 points are constructed as seven antipodal pairs, so the diameter is exactly fixed  │
│                          │ by construction and the problem becomes a 7-line Grassmannian packing problem in 3D:      │
│                          │ minimize the largest absolute inner product between seven unit directions.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A batched Riemannian soft-max optimization searches many line-packings simultaneously on  │
│                          │ the product of spheres. It is followed by an exact hard-coherence coordinate search that  │
│                          │ only accepts improvements to the true minimum-distance/diameter ratio. This removes       │
│                          │ translation, scale, diameter handling, and half of the point variables from the numerical │
│                          │ search.                                                                                   │
