│                          │ formulation.  Normalize the incumbent so its closest squared distance is one, then        │
│                          │ minimize an explicit diameter variable subject to every pairwise squared distance being   │
│                          │ at least one and at most that diameter.  This is the direct epigraph formulation of the   │
│                          │ evaluator objective, unlike the earlier softmin/softmax surrogate.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The analytic constraint Jacobian makes SLSQP practical despite the 91 pair constraints.   │
│                          │ Two passes are used: the first permits a minute lower-bound relaxation to settle the      │
│                          │ active contact graph, while the second uses the exact lower bound and tighter             │
│                          │ termination.  The result is accepted only if it is numerically feasible and improves the  │
│                          │ exact ratio, retaining the robust stochastic incumbent otherwise.                         │
