│ patch_description        │ The prior program uses 10 equal 4,600-step Adam searches, followed by three SLSQP polish  │
│                          │ attempts and stochastic exact-ratio moves. Its main parameters are the beta continuation  │
│                          │ `8→528`, Adam coefficients `(0.89, 0.995)`, initial learning rate `0.026`, 10 restarts,   │
│                          │ and 1,100 SLSQP iterations.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version replaces equal-budget restarts with successive halving: 18 diverse starts    │
│                          │ receive a shorter broad search (`2,000` iterations, beta `6→190`), are ranked using the   │
│                          │ exact squared min/max ratio, and only the best 5 receive a longer sharp contact-graph     │
│                          │ phase (`3,100` iterations, beta `170→950`). This allocates late optimization effort to    │
│                          │ promising basins while increasing initial contact-graph diversity. The final constrained  │
│                          │ fixed-minimum-distance SLSQP formulation is applied to the strongest 5 candidates with    │
│                          │ tighter explicit feasibility polishing. The returned value remains exactly a finite `(14, │
│                          │ 3)` NumPy array.                                                                          │
