│ patch_description        │ Use the recommended feasibility-aware two-pass epigraph refinement. The first SLSQP pass  │
│                          │ has a minute lower-distance relaxation, which allows a nearly active contact graph to     │
│                          │ exchange constraints instead of being locked by floating-point-level violations. Its      │
│                          │ result is then rescaled so its true minimum squared distance is exactly one and used to   │
│                          │ initialize a tighter exact pass. Every returned intermediate configuration is evaluated   │
│                          │ using the evaluator’s actual hard squared ratio, so only a genuine improvement is         │
│                          │ retained.                                                                                 │
