│ patch_name               │ active_contact_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final isotropic random hill climb with an active-contact exact-ratio polish.  │
│                          │ Near a diameter-packing optimum, only pairs close to the current minimum and maximum      │
│                          │ distances determine the nonsmooth objective.  The new stage explicitly forms separating   │
│                          │ forces from short contacts and contracting forces from long contacts, then selects pure   │
│                          │ or mixed projected moves based on contact-count imbalance.  Every move is still accepted  │
│                          │ only when the exact squared min/max ratio improves.  A small random tangent proposal      │
│                          │ remains available to escape contact-graph degeneracies, while adaptive contact width and  │
│                          │ proposal scale make the stage increasingly local after improvements stall.                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
